# Hermes Agent — environment.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.hermes/.env and fill in your key.
#
# COST CAP — Prepaid credits only, auto-recharge OFF.
# Hermes calls LLMs over the network; running out of credit is the hard
# cost ceiling. Funding the OpenRouter balance with prepaid credits (no
# auto-recharge) means the worst case is "Hermes stops working", not
# "I wake up to a $400 bill". Never enable auto top-up.
#
# Upstream's full env reference (90+ providers) is at:
#   https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/blob/main/.env.example
# Only the OpenRouter stanza is enabled here; uncomment others if needed.

# =============================================================================
# LLM PROVIDER (OpenRouter) — default
# =============================================================================
# OpenRouter routes to ~200 models behind a single key. Pick the per-task
# model via `hermes model` or in ~/.hermes/config.yaml (model.default).
# Get a key at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Long-term memory vault (read by the bundled `obsidian` skill)
# =============================================================================
# The skill at skills/note-taking/obsidian/ uses normal file tools against
# this path. No Obsidian app required — any markdown editor works. On this
# host the vault is also a Syncthing share, so edits replicate to other
# devices. See modules/hermes-agent/install.sh for the scaffolded layout.
#
# Hardcoded absolute path: python-dotenv's shell-variable expansion is
# version/loader-dependent. Update if you ever run hermes as a non-`ms` user.
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/home/ms/hermes-vault
